"""Original English conversations, with preassigned scenario groups."""
ROWS=[]
def add(family,group,*turns):ROWS.append(dict(family=family,group=group,turns=turns))
add('correction','negative_to_positive_rsvp',
('I told Zoya I could not come to her exhibition. My plans changed and I can go now.','You can let her know the new answer without pretending you never declined: “My plans changed, and I can come to your exhibition after all.”'),
('Add that I will arrive after the opening speech.','My plans changed, and I can come to your exhibition after all. I will arrive after the opening speech.'),
('Is that a promise to attend the speech?','No. It says you will arrive after the speech.'),
('She asks whether I am still unable to come. Give a direct reply.','I can come now. I will arrive after the opening speech.'))
add('correction','restoration_not_replacement',
('I want to replace the faded cover of my family album. Help me ask a craft shop.','Could you help me replace the faded cover of my family album?'),
('No, I want to keep the original cover and repair it if possible. Replace was the wrong word.','Could you assess whether the original cover of my family album can be repaired? I would like to keep it rather than replace it.'),
('Do not promise the repair is possible.','The wording asks them to assess it. It does not claim that repair is possible.'),
('They ask whether I want a completely new cover.','No, I would prefer to keep and repair the original cover if that is possible.'),
('What is the main preference behind this request?','Preserving the original cover rather than replacing it.'))
add('correction','quote_speaker_retracted',
('My notes attribute “We need more time” to the chair.','Your notes record the chair as saying, “We need more time.”'),
('I am no longer sure who said it. The words are accurate, but the speaker is uncertain.','Keep the quotation, but mark the speaker as uncertain rather than assigning it to the chair.'),
('Can I write the whole committee agreed?','No. An unidentified speaker’s comment does not establish agreement by the whole committee.'),
('Give me an honest note for the minutes draft.','“We need more time” was said during the discussion; the speaker has not been identified.'))
add('correction','audience_shift_children',
('Explain a library catalogue to an adult learning English.','A library catalogue is a list of the books and other items a library has. You can search it to find an item and see where it is kept.'),
('Actually this is for a child visiting a library for the first time.','A library catalogue helps you find things in the library. If you want a book about dinosaurs, you can search for dinosaurs and see which books the library has.'),
('Keep the child-friendly example, but do not assume they like dinosaurs.','If you want a book about a topic you enjoy, you can search for that topic in the catalogue and see what the library has.'),
('Does changing the audience change what a catalogue is?','No. It changes the explanation and examples, not what the catalogue does.'))
add('correction','same_name_two_people',
('There are two people called Alex in our club. Alex Chen takes photographs, and Alex Rao writes the newsletter.','Use their surnames when assigning jobs: Alex Chen handles photographs, and Alex Rao writes the newsletter.'),
('Alex Rao will take photographs at this event too. Chen is still taking them as well.','For this event, both Alex Chen and Alex Rao will take photographs. Rao also has the newsletter role you described.'),
('Please tell Alex to bring a camera.','Which Alex should the message go to: Chen, Rao, or both?'),
('Both.','Alex Chen and Alex Rao, please bring your cameras for the event.'),
('Did Rao replace Chen?','No. You said Rao would take photographs too, while Chen would continue.'))
add('correction','borrow_vs_give',
('I gave my neighbour a ladder for the weekend. Write a note asking for it back.','Could you return my ladder after the weekend, please?'),
('I meant lent, not gave permanently. Make that clear if needed.','Could you return the ladder I lent you for the weekend, please?'),
('I do not want it to sound as though they have already failed to return it.','The note can simply ask for its return after the weekend, without suggesting it is overdue.'),
('Give me the final note.','Could you return the ladder I lent you after the weekend, please?'))
add('correction','draft_diagnosis_removed',
('My laptop will not start. Draft a message to a repair shop saying the battery is broken.','Unless you know the battery is the cause, it is better to describe the symptom: “My laptop will not start. Could you inspect it and tell me what is wrong?”'),
('You are right. I only know that it will not start.','Then keep the message about that symptom and let the shop investigate the cause.'),
('It sometimes starts when connected to power. Add that observation, not a diagnosis.','My laptop will not start reliably, though it sometimes starts when connected to power. Could you inspect it and tell me what is wrong?'),
('Can we now say the battery is definitely broken?','No. That observation may help the repair shop, but it does not establish a definite cause.'))
add('correction','two_stage_deadline',
('The club wants topic suggestions by Monday and the final programme by Friday.','Monday is the deadline for topic suggestions; Friday is the deadline for the final programme.'),
('They moved the suggestions deadline to Tuesday. The final programme deadline did not move.','Topic suggestions are now due Tuesday. The final programme is still due Friday.'),
('Write a reminder that only asks people for suggestions.','Please send your topic suggestions by Tuesday.'),
('Someone thinks the whole programme is due Tuesday.','You can clarify that Tuesday is only for suggestions. The final programme remains due Friday.'),
('What changed from the original schedule?','The topic-suggestion deadline moved from Monday to Tuesday.'))
add('memory','school_story_fiction_label',
('I am writing a fictional school newsletter for a class exercise. The imaginary school is called Meadow School. Do not present it as a real report.','We can label it as a fictional newsletter for the exercise and use Meadow School as the invented setting.'),
('Include a story about pupils creating a reading corner.','In this fictional edition, pupils at Meadow School have created a reading corner where classmates can sit and share books.'),
('Give it a warm headline.','A New Corner for Shared Stories'),
('Add a short quotation from an invented pupil, but label it as invented too.','Invented pupil quotation: “I like having a quiet place to sit with a book.”'),
('Someone wants to cite this as evidence that a real school opened a reading space. Is that valid?','No. The school and report were invented for a class exercise.'),
('Can we still use it in the class display?','Yes, as fictional work, with that label clear.'),
('What name did we give the imaginary school?','Meadow School.'))
add('memory','museum_sketch_permission',
('The museum allows pencil sketches but says no ink pens. I am taking a pencil and a small sketchbook.','That fits the rule you shared: pencil sketches are allowed, while ink pens are not.'),
('I want to sketch one object slowly rather than rush around.','Choosing one object can give you time to notice its shape and details. You do not need to fill the sketchbook during a single visit.'),
('Help me ask where I can sit without blocking anyone.','Is there somewhere I can sit to sketch without blocking the walkway?'),
('They might say there is no seating. Give me a polite reply if that happens.','Thanks for letting me know. I will choose a spot where I can stand without getting in the way.'),
('My friend offers me an ink pen because it draws darker lines. Should I use it under the rule I mentioned?','No. The museum rule you shared permits pencil sketches but not ink pens.'))
add('memory','friend_no_surprise_visit',
('I want to cheer up my friend, but they asked me not to arrive without checking first.','You can offer company by message and let them decide. That respects their request while still showing that you care.'),
('I could bring a book they wanted to borrow.','You could mention the book as part of the offer, without making it a reason to turn up unannounced.'),
('Draft the message without asking them to explain why they might say no.','Would you like some company? I could bring the book you wanted to borrow. No worries if today does not suit you.'),
('No reply yet. I am tempted to just leave the book in person.','Wait for their reply or ask about a suitable way to pass it on. They specifically asked you to check before arriving.'),
('Is their silence the same as accepting the visit?','No. You have not received agreement to a visit.'),
('I will wait. Could I send a long explanation of why I want to help?','You can keep it brief. A long explanation may create pressure to respond; the invitation you sent already makes the offer clear.'),
('What boundary did they set at the start?','Check with them before arriving; do not make a surprise visit.'))
add('memory','harbour_drawing_limits',
('I want to draw a harbour from imagination. No people and no boats; focus on the buildings and water.','You could show waterfront buildings reflected in the water, with empty mooring posts and a stretch of quay. That keeps the harbour setting without adding people or boats.'),
('It should be early morning, with soft light.','Use pale light on the buildings and gentle reflections rather than sharp midday shadows.'),
('I am not confident drawing windows in detail.','You can suggest groups of windows with simple dark shapes instead of drawing every frame. Keep the main building shapes clear.'),
('Would a busy crowd improve it?','It would change your brief. You asked for no people and wanted the buildings and water to be the focus.'),
('Then give me a short drawing brief with all the constraints.','An imagined harbour in soft early-morning light, focused on buildings and water. No people or boats; keep window details simple.'))
add('memory','waiting_list_not_ticket',
('I joined the waiting list for the lecture. I do not have a ticket yet.','You are on the waiting list, which is not the same as having a confirmed ticket.'),
('I want to tell my colleague I hope to go.','I am on the waiting list for the lecture, so I hope I will be able to go.'),
('They ask if we can meet there.','You can say you would like to, but that your attendance depends on getting a ticket.'),
('I will ask about the topic in the meantime. Draft a question.','Could you share a little more about what the lecture will cover?'),
('Do not invent a topic for that question.','The question asks what the lecture covers without assuming a topic.'),
('No one has replied with a ticket offer. Can I call myself a confirmed attendee in my message?','No. Your place has not been confirmed.'),
('If I later receive a ticket, what should change in the message?','You can then say you have a ticket and confirm whether you plan to attend.'),
('What is my current status, not the hypothetical later one?','On the waiting list, without a confirmed ticket.'))
add('memory','map_symbol_meanings',
('On the map I drew, a square means a bench and a circle means a drinking fountain. These are my own symbols.','For your map, squares mark benches and circles mark drinking fountains.'),
('I want a simple legend.','Square: bench\nCircle: drinking fountain'),
('The map is for visitors who may not know the area. What else could make it easier to read?','You could label the main entrance and show which way is north, if you know the orientation.'),
('I know the entrance, but I am unsure about north.','Label the entrance, and leave out a north arrow until you can confirm the direction.'),
('A visitor points to a circle. What does that mean on this map?','A drinking fountain.'),
('Is that necessarily what a circle means on every map?','No. It is the convention you chose for this map.'),
('Can you now tell them what the square means too?','A square marks a bench.'))
add('memory','reading_glasses_not_sunglasses',
('My reading glasses are in the bedside drawer. My sunglasses are in the car.','Reading glasses: bedside drawer. Sunglasses: car.'),
('I want to read a letter later, but first I need to reply to a dinner invitation.','You can deal with the invitation first. What do you want the reply to say?'),
('I can attend, but I will leave early.','Thank you for inviting me. I can come, though I will need to leave early.'),
('Make it more casual.','Thanks for the invite! I can come, but I will need to leave early.'),
('Done. Where did I say the glasses for reading were?','In the bedside drawer.'),
('The car has glasses too. Are those the same pair?','No. You said the sunglasses are in the car.'),
('Did I mention putting either pair into a bag?','No. You did not mention moving either pair into a bag.'))
add('memory','camera_no_people',
('I am taking pictures of the craft stall. The organiser asked me not to include visitors’ faces.','Focus on the crafts and stall details, and frame the shots so visitors’ faces are not included.'),
('I like close-ups of the woven baskets.','Close-ups of the baskets fit that brief and can show the texture clearly.'),
('The sign in the background is crooked. Should I ask before moving it?','Yes. Ask the organiser rather than rearranging their stall without checking.'),
('They said I can straighten the sign.','You can straighten the sign within that permission. It does not change the photography restriction.'),
('Now a visitor smiles at the stall. Can I assume the organiser’s rule is cancelled?','No. The instruction not to include visitors’ faces still applies.'),
('Give me a caption for the basket photo without pretending I made it.','A close look at the woven baskets on the craft stall.'),
('Which permission did I actually receive?','Permission to straighten the sign, not to include visitors’ faces.'))
